    <item>
      <title>Visible Rauru's arm for all armors</title>
      <author>Mellamocarlos</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/453232</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/453232#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">fe9d3113819f6d70dfa9553aad705bef9a52ee94</guid>
      <pubDate>Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:33:26 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecc27b929f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8f84e76.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8f840a8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8f9200c.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8f98846.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fa38b3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8f8f280.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fa692f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fa342f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fa884f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fae1c4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fb8c5e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fb1ff8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fbfacd.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8f9fcc8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fbecf8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fc3a88.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8f935d1.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fc795f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/649ecd8fa7301.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Fixed Broken Link&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Now you should be able to download the mod&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Visible Rauru's Arm for all Armors&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Makes almost ALL the armors in the game to show Rauru's arm when you wear them, i excluded some  that I feel wouldn't make sense, like the Flamebreaker set (i guessed Rauru's arm isn't fireproof) and the Yiga one (it's a disguise) for example.&lt;br&gt;My other mod: &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/451537"&gt;Promotional Champion's Leathers&lt;/a&gt; is included within this mod, so i recommend deleting it if you want to play with this one.&lt;br&gt;This is a comprehensive change to the game so if I missed anything or something isn't working properly don't be afraid to tell me.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;To install it just move the folder corresponding to your version of the game to the mod directory in your emulator.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Compatibility with other mods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you have any other mods that modify the Resource Table (If they have &lt;span class="RedColor SelectedElement"&gt;ResourceSizeTable.Product.XXX.rsizetable.zs&lt;/span&gt; file inside System/Resource folders) you will need to make them the same as the one in my mod and the ones in this mod the same to the other one, you can make both files the same (put the values of the entries from the other mod in the RSTB of mine and viceversa) or my recomendation is to look for the values the other mod changes (should be in their mod page), change the values of those entries in the RSTB of my mod and then delete de RSTB of the other mod.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For example if you wanted to change the values of an armor you would need to look for  &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Armor_XXX.Armor_XXX_RaulSkin_Upper.bfres  &lt;/span&gt;in the resource table and change the entry value to the one the modder says it should be.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The last column of the Spredsheet below has the value changes i made in the RSTB.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Guide for removing individual Armors&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In case you don't like any specific armor of this mod and want to go back to the original one but keep the rest of them you should do the next:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;For example, let's imagine you want to keep the original &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Tunic of the Wild.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Go to this &lt;a href="https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1dIg7ORBFJOK8g9IJIwQcX9RIDISwLx0RMwBA-aTxfgc/edit#gid=0" target="_blank"&gt;Spreadsheet&lt;/a&gt; I made with all the necesary values.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. Look up the &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;ActorName &lt;/span&gt;of the armor you want to remove in the Spreadsheet, in this case it's &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Armor_005_RaulSkin_Upper&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, go to the &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;romfs/Model&lt;/span&gt; folder in the mod and look for the file that has that name and delete it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. Now you need to check the &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Pack Files &lt;/span&gt;of the armor, there are usually 5 (one for each upgrade) but if the armor can't be upgraded there will only be one, in this case, for the &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;Tunic of the Wild&lt;/span&gt; they are &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Armor_005_Upper.pack.zs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Armor_035_Upper.pack.zs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Armor_039_Upper.pack.zs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Armor_060_Upper.pack.zs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; and &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Armor_061_Upper.pack.zs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;, look for them inside the &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;romfs/Pack/Actor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;folder and remove them.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. And the last one, using &lt;a href="https://github.com/NX-Editor/NxEditor" target="_blank"&gt;NX Editor&lt;/a&gt; and the hash table from the Research channel in the &lt;a href="https://discord.gg/bgZDNQ6sF2" target="_blank"&gt;modding discord&lt;/a&gt;, open the Resource table (&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;ResourceSizeTable.Product.XXX.rzisetable.zs&lt;/span&gt; inside &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;romfs/System/Resource&lt;/span&gt; folder) and look for the armor you want to remove with the prefix Model/ and the start of the &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;ActorName &lt;/span&gt; of the respective armor, in this case it would be &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Model/Armor_005&lt;/span&gt;,and make sure to choose the one that ends with &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;upper&lt;/span&gt;, you will see that the value is something like &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;500000 &lt;/span&gt; for example, now you need to look for the original Resource Table Value in the Spreadsheet (for this armor it's &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;190016&lt;/span&gt;) and change the value to that.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. You are done, enjoy!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The only thing i feel is missing from this mod is some custom icons for the armors, if someone want to make that happen, hit me up (I have my Discord in my profile) and we can get to work on it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/visible_raurus_arm.zip" type="application/zip"/>
      <category>Player</category>
      <category>Models</category>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Ordeal of the Demon King - Two New Quests</title>
      <author>- Tarnagh -</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">a4053cd402d89d854690a167c350f5042cde147a</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 17:45:17 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa97c7cc229e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9dae19baf40.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa97c8b8ae97.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a96fae3ed1b9.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; v2.1.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Bugfix&lt;/em&gt;: Fix some bugs&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: now, Ganondorf can teleport the player (see description)&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Created by &lt;strong&gt;Tarnagh&lt;/strong&gt;. Bow model and texture by &lt;strong&gt;The Hidden Yiga Clan&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Ordeal of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"You have faced monsters, Dragons, and gods. But have you ever stood before the Demon King himself?"&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Ganondorf stands, and he is waiting for you. Not for a battle - but for an answer. He has watched the bearer of the Master Sword from afar, counted his victories, and now he intends to find out for himself whether the hero is worth anything at all.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This is a full quest line: dialogue, choices that stick, a duel of his choosing, two commissions that end with weapons no one else in Hyrule can give you - and, for those who survive him, paths no one else can open.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
He offers you a choice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Kneel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Or refuse.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose carefully. The Demon King does not offer his mercy twice.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Ordeal&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Those who bow before him earn something granted to almost no one: the chance to prove themselves in single combat, against an opponent he picks personally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Survive, and he will admit - grudgingly, in his own way - that you are more than another hero clinging to a dying world. Refuse the duel, and the ordeal ends where it began, beneath his gaze.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The King's Will&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A proven hero is a useful hero, and the Demon King has work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
His first commission sends you after the horns of three Silver Lynels, thirty of Naydra's spikes, and a horn taken from the Light Dragon herself. Bring them, and he will forge you a bow out of them, by hand, in front of you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Watch closely as their fragile light is consumed by my darkness."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
And the world answers him. While he forges, gloom boils up around him and the sky and earth turn the red of a Blood Moon - and when the rite is done, the colour drains away again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
But do not mistake his favour for friendship. You serve his purpose for exactly as long as you remain useful.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Horn of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Take this. A horn of my true form. A manifestation of the doom that awaits this fragile world."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Come back to him carrying his bow and he will ask more of you - if you are willing to hear it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This time he wants the horns of all three elemental Dragons, and two from the Light Dragon. What he makes of them is not a weapon but a piece of one: &lt;strong&gt;a shard of the form he has not yet taken&lt;/strong&gt;, fused from their elemental essence and his own dark magic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Fuse it to anything you like:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;+90 attack&lt;/strong&gt; - well past anything the base game offers&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fire in every form&lt;/strong&gt; - it sets what it strikes alight, explodes in flame, keeps you warm, and does not go out&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shatters armour&lt;/strong&gt;, fells trees, and throws further&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;On a shield: &lt;strong&gt;guard bonus, perfect-parry bonus, shield bash and counter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
It cannot be sold. Some things are not for rupees.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;New: The Demon King's Path&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Name a place, then the ground between here and it will cease to matter."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Once his trial is behind you and his first commission given, your conversations with him can end with a request: &lt;strong&gt;open a way for me&lt;/strong&gt;. He answers with the same dark rite he forges with - and then the world folds, and you are somewhere else.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Seven places, some of them closed to you any other way:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Old Throne Room&lt;/strong&gt; - the Sanctum in Hyrule Castle&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Floating Coliseum&lt;/strong&gt; - five Lynels, and the Depths all around&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Thunderhead Isles&lt;/strong&gt; - the storm that hides the relics of the Zonai&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt; - the very tomb of the prologue, where he was sealed&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath Hyrule Castle&lt;/strong&gt; - Gloom's Approach, the heart of his malice&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; - below the Depths themselves, where there is nothing at all&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Western Plateau&lt;/strong&gt; - ground beyond the walls Hyrule raised to keep its world small&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A few words of warning, because he will not give you any:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;In the &lt;strong&gt;Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt;, do not walk on towards the Demon King's own cutscene. Leave the way you would leave anywhere else - by the map.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; means exactly that.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;You may arrive on gloom. Do not let it take away your life.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King:&lt;/strong&gt; Ganondorf as he ought to be - imposing, calculating, merciless, and worthy of the title. His words are written in red.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choices that stick:&lt;/strong&gt; what you say to him is remembered across saves, and he remembers it too.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The King's Trial:&lt;/strong&gt; a duel against an opponent he chooses for you, with miasma.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two commissions:&lt;/strong&gt; hunt across Hyrule for materials no shop sells, and watch him forge them by hand - gloom, sound and a blood-red sky included.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two unique rewards:&lt;/strong&gt; a bow of his own making, and the Horn of the Demon King.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King's Road:&lt;/strong&gt; seven destinations across the surface, the sky, the Depths, and places the game never meant you to reach.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No new NPC clutter:&lt;/strong&gt; one existing character carries the whole thing. Nothing else in the world is moved.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Begin the Ordeal&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Find him north of the Gerudo Canyon Pass, west of the Rakakudaj Shrine.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Approach, and hear his demand.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Kneel - or refuse.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;If you are still standing, decide whether to accept his trial.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Win it, and take his first commission.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Return with his bow in hand, and ask him for more.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;At the end of any conversation, ask him to open a way.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Installation&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TKCL / TKMM:&lt;/strong&gt; import the file and enable the mod.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manual:&lt;/strong&gt; unpack the ZIP so that &lt;code&gt;romfs&lt;/code&gt; lands in&lt;br&gt;&#13;
      &lt;code&gt;atmosphere/contents/0100F2C0115B6000/romfs/&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emulator:&lt;/strong&gt; place the same &lt;code&gt;romfs&lt;/code&gt; folder in the game's mod directory.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Specifications&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;For developers and modders:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Host actor:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Npc_BaseCampSoldier_Hylia005&lt;/em&gt; - renamed, re-scripted, and given Ganondorf's pack. No new actor is registered.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quest logic:&lt;/strong&gt; EventFlow, in his own flowchart - branches, talk choices, pouch queries and autosaves.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Persistence:&lt;/strong&gt; six booleans appended to &lt;em&gt;GameDataList&lt;/em&gt;, with &lt;em&gt;MetaData&lt;/em&gt; resized to match so they actually reach &lt;em&gt;progress.sav&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dialogue:&lt;/strong&gt; Mals, built from genuine vanilla 1.2.0 archives. His lines carry the inline red colour code; your choices stay white.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teleportation:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;GameSystemActor.EventReserveBancChange&lt;/em&gt; by named start position. Two are vanilla (&lt;em&gt;OpeningStart&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;StartPos_HyruleCastleIncident&lt;/em&gt;); five are added to the &lt;em&gt;MainField&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;MinusField&lt;/em&gt; start-position tables. The menu is three steps of four choices - the most a single talk event can show.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; Crystallized Ice Bow (&lt;em&gt;Weapon_Bow_166_For_Ganondorf&lt;/em&gt;), Horn of the Demon King (&lt;em&gt;Item_Enemy_39&lt;/em&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource table:&lt;/strong&gt; every entry the mod grows is recomputed and shipped.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;The Ordeal Awaits&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;Stand before the Demon King. Prove your worth. And remember - he is the one deciding whether you deserve to live.&lt;/em&gt;</description>
