ebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437836292.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e4377c684f.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e4378694ff.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e4375a35d3.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437169355.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e436f927d5.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e4374934a6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e43719262d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437055f52.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437731f4a.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437a2047d.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e4379c52ce.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437a6b6e4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437aa6a37.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437a68764.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e4379e2011.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437875083.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e4377bfb47.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437805bdc.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e43712a249.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6a9e437664294.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; 2.0.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Overhaul&lt;/em&gt;: Overhauled the entire mod to merge options properly via TKMM, so no presets are needed&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added Increased Bloom option, as well as Normal Bloom and Bloom Disabled&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added Darkest Nighttime Lighting option, in addition to Normal and Darker options previously seen&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added Brighter Daytime Lighting option, in addition to Normal Daytime Lighting previously seen&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added 2 new Overworld Fog options, including Increased and Maximum Overworld Fog&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added 2 new Sky Fog options, including Increased and Maximum Sky Fog&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added a new Cave Lighting options, including Darker, Darkest, Normal and Brighter Cave options&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new Cave Fog options, including Normal Fog and Increased Fog, as well as Reduced Fog which was seen previously&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new Indoor Fog options - Indoor Fog disabled (seen previously) and enabled&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added 3 new Light Brightness options, including Dimmer, Normal and Brighter Lights&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added 2 new options to customize how sky biomes are distributed&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new Cloud Opacity options, with 5 different new options to choose from&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new Cloud Density options, with 5 different new options to choose from&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new Cloud Size options, with 5 different new options to choose from&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new Cloud Speed options, with 5 different new options to choose from&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new Cloud Line Height options, allowing you to choose from normal cloud height and raised cloud height to see clouds above The Sky layer itself&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Adjustment&lt;/em&gt;: Some biomes under the "Darker Nights" category have been reworked and adjusted to match the option better&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Addition&lt;/em&gt;: Added new biome to Tabantha Depths, seen in Depths of the Kingdom's 2.0 update under the "Vanilla+" option&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;Hyrule Rebeautified has now reached version 2.0.0, and is now fully customizable through TKMM. Gone are the days where there were set presets for the mod. At it's core, it features new biomes in every region of the game, including Eldin, Hebra, Gerudo, Akkala, Faron and Lanayru, as well as corresponding unique regions in The Depths (featuring work from Depths of the Kingdom). However now, you can FULLY CUSTOMIZE how you want your game to look. Due to the complex nature of the rework of the mod, it can only be used via TKMM. Screenshots of each option's affect can be found on the dedicated TKCL file. This mod works with all versions of TOTK that support mods, and works on both emulator and Switch.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Options include:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Surface Fog - allows you to choose between reduced, normal, increased and maximum surface fog. Affects how well you can see into the distance&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sky Fog - allows you to choose how well you want to see from The Sky. This includes reduced, normal, increased and maximum options. Lower options mean you can see the surface below well, but Maximum? You can't see The Surface at all!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cave Fog - allows you to control how much fog is in caves. The options include reduced, normal, and increased fog for caves.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Indoor Fog - allows you to choose between indoor fog enabled and no indoor fog.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Daytime Lighting - allows you to control how bright you want mornings, daytime and evenings to be. You can choose between normal daytime lighting and brighter daytime lighting. Brighter lighting has extra palettes added to the timetable to ensure smooth transitions even between brighter days and the darkest nights if those options are selected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nighttime Lighting - Allows you to control how dark you want your nights to be. You can choose between normal, darker, and darkest nighttime lighting presets. The darkest one makes it even darker than The Depths, so bring those brightblooms ready if you want a scary experience!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cave Lighting - Allows you to customize how bright and dark you want the caves to be in the game. You can choose between normal caves, brighter caves, darker caves, and darkest caves. If choosing the 2 darker cave options, this overwrites the cave fog settings because black fog is used to make it feel like you are in Nutty Putty Cave: Hyrule Edition&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sky Biome Zones - the game only has a certain number of climates, meaning that for sky regions to have their own unique biomes (shared with the surface), new ones couldn't be created. Overworld and Sky fog levels are consistent with each other, so 2 options are available here to allow you to prioritize unique colors per region in The Sky, or being able to have different fog levels independently properly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Light Brightness - Lights in the game can be customized between dimmer, normal, and increased brightness levels&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Bloom -  Allows you to customize the soft glow in the game, choosing between no bloom, normal bloom and increased bloom. Bloom is not recommended with the Brighter Daytime Lighting option or pairing with Depths of the Kingdom&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cloud Density - allows you to control how many clouds are in the sky. You can choose between 5 different levels&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cloud Opacity - allows you to control how transparent the clouds are. There are 5 different levels. No cloud opacity = no clouds in the sky&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cloud Size - allows you to control how big the clouds are. There are 5 different levels&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cloud Line Height - allows you to control how high up the clouds are. Normal Cloud Line is similar to the original game where clouds aren't visible in The Sky and only The Surface. Raised Cloud Line allows you to actually see the clouds in The Sky and raises the position of all the clouds!</description>
